y but not automatically Democratic.", "watch": "A last-week national environment shift or effective consolidation of law-and-order messaging behind Demuth could compress the polling lead.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's governorship is open after Tim Walz chose not to seek another term, and Democrats turned to Senator Amy Klobuchar, a three-time statewide winner, while Republicans nominated House minority leader Lisa Demuth. Minnesota leans Democratic by about three points, and Klobuchar enters the final stretch with clear edges in money and recognition. Recent polls from SurveyUSA, the Star Tribune/KARE 11, and Morning Consult show her leading by seven to nine points, with earlier surveys wider. Race ratings cluster between Likely Democratic and Solid Democratic, and prediction markets put her odds above ninety percent.\n\nDemuth has centered her campaign on gang violence and public safety and recently gained Mike Lindell's endorsement, but she was fact-checked on insulin pricing votes and trails badly in fundraising, with about $3.9 million cash for Klobuchar versus roughly half a million for Demuth. A minimally funded Green nominee is also on the ballot.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9491, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9656, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9546, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9536, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9443, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9461, "margin": 9.0}, {"d